meta-streaming
==============

OpenHD-based camera streaming images for Raspberry Pi, built with
OpenEmbedded/BitBake (OE-Core release "wrynose").

This workspace is assembled with `repo` and contains these layers:

  openembedded-core   OE-Core (provides meta/, oe-init-build-env)
  meta-openembedded   meta-oe, meta-python, meta-networking
  meta-raspberrypi    Raspberry Pi BSP
  meta-qt5            Qt5
  meta-openhd         OpenHD
  meta-streaming      this layer (recipes, multiconfigs, build config)

Note: OE-Core does not bundle BitBake or the `poky` distro. BitBake is cloned
into the workspace on first build, and the build uses the OE-Core default
distro (DISTRO = ""). Both the native and Docker instructions below handle this.


Targets
=======

Images are built as BitBake multiconfigs (meta-streaming/conf/multiconfig/):

  mc:air-rpi0:core-image-minimal      air unit, Raspberry Pi Zero
  mc:air-rpi4:core-image-minimal      air unit, Raspberry Pi 4 (64-bit)
  mc:ground-rpi4:core-image-minimal   ground unit, Raspberry Pi 4 (64-bit)


Build with Docker (recommended)
===============================

The container provides a known-good Ubuntu build host, so no host setup is
needed beyond Docker. The Dockerfile and wrapper script live in
meta-streaming/conf/templates/streaming/.

From the workspace root:

  ./meta-streaming/conf/templates/streaming/build-streaming.sh            # air-rpi4 (default)
  ./meta-streaming/conf/templates/streaming/build-streaming.sh air-rpi0
  ./meta-streaming/conf/templates/streaming/build-streaming.sh ground-rpi4

The script builds the `streaming-yocto` image (as an unprivileged user matching
your UID/GID), fetches BitBake, writes build/conf, and runs the multiconfig
target. Build output lands in ./build/ (shared with the host via a bind mount).


Build natively on Ubuntu
========================

Tested on Ubuntu 22.04. BitBake must not be run as root.

1. Install the required host packages:

     sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y \
         gawk wget git diffstat unzip texinfo gcc build-essential chrpath \
         socat cpio python3 python3-pip python3-pexpect xz-utils debianutils \
         iputils-ping python3-git python3-jinja2 python3-subunit zstd \
         liblz4-tool file locales libacl1 bzip2 ccache rsync kmod

2. Ensure a UTF-8 locale:

     sudo locale-gen en_US.UTF-8
     export LANG=en_US.UTF-8 LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8

3. From the workspace root, clone BitBake (once); the 2.18 branch matches
   OE-Core's BB_MIN_VERSION:

     [ -d bitbake ] || git clone --branch 2.18 --single-branch \
         https://git.openembedded.org/bitbake bitbake

4. Initialise the build environment:

     source openembedded-core/oe-init-build-env build

5. Write build/conf/bblayers.conf for this layer layout (the shipped
   bblayers.conf.sample references poky-only layers that are not present):

     cat > conf/bblayers.conf <<'EOF'
     POKY_BBLAYERS_CONF_VERSION = "2"
     BBPATH = "${TOPDIR}"
     BBFILES ?= ""
     BBLAYERS ?= " \
       ${TOPDIR}/../openembedded-core/meta \
       ${TOPDIR}/../meta-openembedded/meta-oe \
       ${TOPDIR}/../meta-openembedded/meta-python \
       ${TOPDIR}/../meta-openembedded/meta-networking \
       ${TOPDIR}/../meta-raspberrypi \
       ${TOPDIR}/../meta-openhd \
       ${TOPDIR}/../meta-streaming \
       ${TOPDIR}/../meta-qt5 \
       "
     EOF

6. Seed build/conf/local.conf from this layer's sample and select the OE-Core
   default distro (poky.conf is not present in this workspace):

     cp ../meta-streaming/conf/templates/streaming/local.conf.sample conf/local.conf
     echo 'DISTRO = ""' >> conf/local.conf

7. Build a target:

     bitbake mc:air-rpi4:core-image-minimal

Images are written under build/tmp-<multiconfig>/deploy/images/.


Adding the layer to an existing build
======================================

  bitbake-layers add-layer meta-streaming
